Z||000000||kornholio||01-13-2001||01:53 PM||||I think I have found what has been causing my blown fuse.  Looks like my trunk light +ve terminal has been touching the metal part of the trunk.  If the +ve touches the metal it blows the fuse, right?  With a blown fuse and the +ve still touching the metal, will that turn on my floor lights?  theogre said something about a sneak feed, so I was wondering if that had anything to do with it.  I don't have a clue how to read the electrical diagrams.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||01-13-2001||01:57 PM||||GM uses what is called a "floating ground" system. Usually when a fuse blows it tends to cause wierd things. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||strdream||01-13-2001||03:42 PM||||Kornholio<BR>Where are you from? It helps to know for recomendations.<BR>A long distance diagnosis requiers good communication and terminalagy is critcal. So bear with me if I don't understand you at first.  I don't know what a +ve wire is but I can say that if grounding it makes dome ligths come on than it is compleating a circuit. thus not likey to be the cause for blown fuses.<BR>If you have wire diagrams you could fax (616-795-3104) to me and I would be glad to work thru it with you on the phone (616-795-3100).<BR>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000003||kornholio||01-13-2001||04:39 PM||||strdream:<BR>I'm in Ontario, Canada.  And by +ve (positive) wire, I meant 12v.  Thanks for your offer.<P>I think that the trunk light was the likely problem.  After I made sure the light didn't short out I replaced the fuse and it has not blown since.<P>I was just wondering if my theory was right:  When the trunk light's 12v wire touches ground it turns on the floor lights after blowing the fuse?||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||01-13-2001||04:56 PM||||kornholio,<BR>Found this exact problem years ago.  Same symptoms, same fix.  Put the 12+ wire in the center of the light when you connect it together.  Mine would fit either way.  <p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||01-15-2001||05:43 PM||||When the Ctsy fuse blows power backfeeds through the floor light elements to ground causing them to light up and the center upper courtesy light not to work.||||reg||1
